-- EXPECT-ERROR: takes `Tagged(_, Realtime)` but also takes `Cap(IO)`
-- Capabilities widening, Task 3 -- Check 7 (`typecheck.ml:5755-5793`),
-- realtime exclusion. `Realtime` is not itself pre-registered in
-- `builtin_types` (`typecheck.ml:1843-1862`); a user declares it as an
-- ordinary nullary ADT (`type Realtime = Realtime`) so `Tagged(Int, Realtime)`
-- resolves as a surface type at all -- Check 7's `is_realtime_tagged`
-- (`typecheck.ml:5760`) matches on the type NAME `"Realtime"` in the second
-- `Tagged` argument, not on any special built-in identity, so a user-declared
-- `Realtime` type satisfies it exactly like a hypothetical built-in one
-- would. `step`'s signature combines a `Tagged(_, Realtime)` parameter with
-- `Cap(IO)` -- one of the three excluded roots (`Alloc`/`IO`/`Panic`,
-- `is_excluded_cap`, `typecheck.ml:5763-5765`) -- which Check 7 forbids:
-- realtime functions cannot hold allocation-, IO-, or panic-capable
-- capabilities. See core-march-types.md §2.8.9.
mod RT do
  type Realtime = Realtime

  needs IO

  fn step(_deadline : Tagged(Int, Realtime), _cap : Cap(IO)) : Int do
    1
  end
end
